.com/users/davidgmbb/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Re-review of **`a0846c8`**, including the merge with the function-lanes implementation (#151), current 9700X results, and the two outstanding comments from my previous review.\n\n**Both previously outstanding findings are fixed:**\n- The raw measurement evidence was migrated out of this repository to the pinned [`buster-performance` record at `2dddeb09`](https://github.com/buster14a/buster-performance/tree/2dddeb09612d54f243cf0521e6bb937cfe2f80f7/docs/measurements/compile-time-518-2026-10-27). I checked that the README identifies the source/compiler revisions, hashes, commands and limitations, and lists `step.log`, `job.log` and checksums. `docs/compile-time.md` now links the immutable external commit and the interim in-repo record was removed, matching AGENTS.md's evidence-storage policy.\n- `check_driver_executable()` now places separate `CHECK_STAGE_DEBUG` and `CHECK_STAGE_PUBLISH_DATA` marks after those operations, so their work no longer inflates the `executable` stage. A direct `-g` fixture with 512 functions/tables exercises both rows, and the two-lane fixture checks a nonzero `lanes` stage and byte-identical object output to the single-lane path.\n\n**Validation at this head:** [9700X run 40482425302](https://github.com/buster14a/buster/actions/runs/40482425302) completed successfully. Its driver suite reports 21,567 checks/0 failures in each of two configurations, including the new timing tests. The stage-attribution step also passes with mandatory tcc-SHA verification and perf counters/profile: 189.004 ms median default compile versus 42.827 ms tcc (4.41×), 0 measurement-harness failures, with `check-input` still the largest stage (~42.4%). This corroborates the pinned earlier baseline without conflating post-#151 measurements with the older snapshot.\n\nI checked the updated one-lane and multi-lane timing boundaries, workflow gating, and archived evidence. **No further actionable correctness or qualification issues found in this pass.** This is a non-approval `COMMENT` review because the authenticated GitHub identity is also the PR's author; I did not run an independent local build.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/buster14a/buster/pull/520#pullrequestreview-5665710015","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/buster14a/buster/pulls/520","author_association":"MEMBER","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/buster14a/buster/pull/520#pullrequestreview-5665710015"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/buster14a/buster/pulls/520"}},"is_copilot_code_review":false,"copilot_code_review_effort":null,"submitted_at":"2026-10-27T10:38:55Z","commit_id":"a0846c8864be41e02404af56594db8e1fa0f14d2"}]